k><name>OKAZAKI, YASUHARU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSURUGA, YASUTAKA</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HAMAMOTO SATOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KANAI TAKASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KAWAMOTO JUNYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAGAO YUKIAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKAZAKI YASUHARU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TSURUGA YASUTAKA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HAMAMOTO, SATOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KANAI, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAWAMOTO, JUNYA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAGAO, YUKIAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKAZAKI, YASUHARU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSURUGA, YASUTAKA</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A hydraulic drive device including a swing control system capable of accelerating it to a stationary state without any jerky swing operation at the time of starting of the swing operation, providing high energy efficiency, forming a stable swing system, and preventing a cost and space from increasing due to provision of additional circuits or complicated problem with circuit configuration from occurring, wherein a pump control device (18) is installed so as to control a discharge flow so that a pump discharge pressure becomes higher by a specified value than the max. load pressures of actuators (2 to 6), pressure compensating valves (12 to 16) are formed so that pressure differences between the discharge pressure of a hydraulic pump (1) and the max. load pressures of the actuators (2 to 6) are set as target compensating pressure differences, respectively, a load dependent characteristic which reduces the target compensating pressure differences when a load pressure rises is provided to the pressure compensating valve (12) of a swing section, and the load dependent characteristic is set so that a flow characteristic simulating the HP constant control of a swing motor can be obtained.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur un entraînement hydraulique comportant un dispositif de contrôle des oscillations: permettant de l'accélérer jusqu'à un état stationnaire en évitant les vibrations brusques au démarrage, à rendement élevé constituant un système vibratoire stable, et évitant les surcoûts et les besoins en espace que nécessiteraient des circuits additionnels et les problèmes d'élaboration de ces circuits. Une pompe de commande (18) règle le flux de décharge de manière à ce que la pression de décharge dépasse d'une valeur donnée la pression maximale de charge des vérins (2 à 6). Des soupapes de compensation de pression (12 à 16) maintiennent le différentiel de pression entre la pression de décharge de la pompe (1) hydraulique et celle des vérins (2 à 6) à une valeur cible de compensation. Les soupapes de compensation de pression (12 à 16) de la zone d'oscillations présentent une caractéristique dépendant de la pression qui réduit le différentiel entre les pressions cibles de compensation lorsque la charge s'élève. La valeur dépendant de la charge est fixée de manière à pouvoir obtenir une caractéristique de flux simulant la commande de haute pression constante d'un moteur oscillant.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>